  "guideSteps": "1. Import a design (JSON / .mcstructure / .schem) — unsupported blocks are listed, the original file is never lost.\n2. Check the 3D preview, layers and floor plans; open Materials to see exact quantities.\n3. Export the design as MCAddon pack (or keep it in the library).\n4. On the phone: open the .mcaddon with Minecraft, activate both packs in the world settings (Beta APIs on).\n5. In game: use the S3D Menu item or chat commands starting with !s3d — preview the hologram, move/rotate/set height, toggle layers & rooms, then build manually or in batches after the confirmation prompt.",
  "@guideSteps": {
    "description": "guideSteps"
  },
  "guideLimitations": "• Android scoped storage prevents writing into Minecraft game folders — the app exports files you open/import manually.\n• Co-located (waterlogged) blocks in .mcstructure files are reported and skipped — v1 formats are single-block-per-cell.\n• Inventory checking in the add-on is only enforced where the Script API can read it; otherwise build proceeds and failures are reported per block.",
  "@guideLimitations": {
    "description": "guideLimitations"
  },
  "guideAddonCommands": "!s3d — open the add-on menu in chat\n!s3d build — start the batch build (asks confirmation first)\n!s3d pause / !s3d resume — pause or resume a running batch\n!s3d speed 32 — set blocks placed per tick (1–256)\n!s3d up / !s3d down — raise/lower the hologram",
  "@guideAddonCommands": {
    "description": "guideAddonCommands"
  }
